					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-404261#post-2067235</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-404261/welcome-to-the-future#post-2067235</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 11 Jul 2014 03:20:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Julian Ashenveil</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1804174</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's possible he did know who they are. He might not have asked what the name was, but rather why they call themselves that. It could've been a little clearer though, but if the question was worded like, say, &quot;Before I go, I've got a question. There's something I've never understood&#8230;why do you call yourselves what you do?&quot; Heck, you could even lop off the bit after the ellipsis, suggesting that the narrator anticipated what the new guy was going to ask.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
